# =============================================================================
# Review markers (use only these two in comments)
# =============================================================================
# ❓  We are not sure (open design choice, ambiguous source/target, needs decision)
# ⏳  Needs validation (proposal written; colleagues should confirm before locking)
# =============================================================================

# Open points:
# - ❓ Is sssom:record_id useful as used here?
# - ⏳ Whole file still needs a review pass
# - ❓ Curation rule for going from a class to another (see contactPoint)?
# - ✅ Variables: one TableGroup per Dataset (aggregates LogicalRecords of the StudyUnit's PIs); not one TG per LogicalProduct
# - ❓ Variables: VariablesInRecord only, or VariableScheme fallback?
# - ❓ propertyUrl: ConceptReference URN vs Concept URI vs DPV-PD (do not invent)?
# - ✅ RecommendedDataType → CSVW built-in name literal (string, integer, …); not XSD IRI (Dedicate #7 / upstream #61)
# - ❓ healthdcatap namespace IRI + hasStructuredData true vs omit when empty?
# - ✅ hasCodeValues: R8 SHACL Literal — emit distinct Code/Value strings (Dedicate #12)
# - ✅ hasCodingSystem: Coding System NAL / Wikidata when known; else local CodeList URN as dct:Standard

# --- Mapping sets --- #

<https://making-sense.info/dedicate/ddi-lifecycle-to-dcat-ap/catalog> a sssom:MappingSet ;
  dcterms:description "Mapping DDI Lifecycle elements to DCAT-AP dataset";
  dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;  # ⏳ Adapt license
  sssom:mapping_provider <https://github.com/Making-Sense-Info/Dedicate/> ;
  sssom:mappings (
  # Catalog mandatory properties
  <https://making-sense.info/dedicate/ddi-lifecycle-to-dcat-ap/catalog/orgname-to-title>
  <https://making-sense.info/dedicate/ddi-lifecycle-to-dcat-ap/catalog/orgname-to-description>
  <https://making-sense.info/dedicate/ddi-lifecycle-to-dcat-ap/catalog/org-to-publisher>
  ) .

